      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## FIXING FACES WITH THIS DETAILER WF:\n\nThis with WAN model is for 81 frames 16fps input.\n\n---\n\ntesting 0.3 denoise (480p in 260 secs) - was too weak on blurry footage.\n\ntesting 0.79 (480p) - still blurry and its changing the characters faces and clothing a bit at this point. \n\ntesting 0.79 (1024 x 576 in 500 secs) - less blurry and might be useable so it stays in context with original when composited back in. but it will change people at that strength so use Wanimate or something to push them back in.\n\nThis workflow worked best at 900p but took a long time and struggled to make it to 81 frames originally. The video I did on it fixing a crowd of faces worked from front to back of the room.\n\nI also experimented with compositing, so taking a small area of an original video, improving it here, then compositing it back into the original. It worked okay but had its own issues, certainly not perfect but LowVRAMs we have to use any trick we can.\n\nWIP.  "
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
