          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "MARKDKBERRY.com:\n\nCONCLUSION- as at 8th Feb 2026 this needs further research for me to be happy with end results for people and faces.\n\n---\n\n# THE BELOW WAS BEFORE I FOUND FLASHVSR\n\n- I am now working with LTX and its best to push that to 720p, before bringing it to a detailer.\n\n- This can handle 16fps up to 157 frames at 480p and takes about 13 mins. More frames than that it craps out (on my 3060) and 157 frames OOMs above it or takes to long.\n\n540p finishing 157 frames @ 16fps in about 17 mins, just about improves faces enough but still not perfect (it also ooms and hangs sometimes). \n\nA run through huMO at that point might sort it. but its banging another 10 mins on (at 480p).\n\ngoing to denoise 0.8 will completely change the result. completely. use up to 0.79 to keep original source video intact.\n\n- Its the best to use if you need to fix faces (denoise 0.79) and you can interpolate back to 24fps on the way out.\n\n- Also try HuMO detailer if you have good quality and just need a polish (gets to 24fps, and maintains consistency, but is limited to 480p for my 3060).\n\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
